{"parentUuid":"962ff48a-04ac-448c-a4e0-e71f78a4b870","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgFiA5HdvJPztLe2Ht843","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01N6Vn1XFqYmMhC2tN2eVgnt","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/vojta/Dev/protocodus.github.io/.claude/worktrees/hedgerow-grass && git status --short && git diff --stat && git add fun/hedgerow/js/ponds.js fun/hedgerow/js/levels/saint-clair.js fun/hedgerow/js/materials.js fun/hedgerow/js/groundmap.js fun/hedgerow/js/main.js fun/hedgerow/README.md && git commit -q -F - <<'EOF'\nHedgerow graphics: rainwater standing in the shell craters\n\nThe craters in the fields south of the village and in the forest were dry\nbowls of mud in the rain. Now the ones that hold water carry a pond\n(ponds.js, new; 31 of the level's 58): a disc at two fifths of the bowl's\ndepth, a little wider than the water so the bowl's own sides and rim cut\nits edge, all in one mesh drawn with the river's water material held\nstill (createWaterMaterial takes a `flow`; zero here): murky, mirroring\nthe sky and the fires, rain rings on it, browner in the shallows and a\nbroken line of scum where it laps the mud, both from its depth in the\nground map. The ground map keeps the grass, the stones and the twigs out\nof the ponds (createGroundMap takes them).\n\nThe level exports its craters (saint-clair.js `craters`: the same list\nthe terrain's bumps are made from, drawn in the same order, so the\nground is unchanged).\n\nThe water's direct specular is capped: the night's fill light is a\ndirectional light, and on still water it made a white-hot moon-like glint\nwherever the view faced it; the lamps and fires are mirrored by the\nscreen-space reflections anyway.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nEOF\ngit log --oneline -1 && (git merge-tree --write-tree --name-only hedgerow-poc hedgerow-grass >/dev/null 2>&1 && echo \"merges cleanly into hedgerow-poc\" || echo \"merge conflicts\")","description":"Commit the crater ponds"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1224,"cache_read_input_tokens":715710,"output_tokens":766,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1224,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":766,"cache_read_input_tokens":715710,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1224,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1224},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01N6Vn1XFqYmMhC2tN2eVgnt":{"command":"cd /Users/vojta/Dev/protocodus.github.io/.claude/worktrees/hedgerow-grass && git status --short && git diff --stat && git add fun/hedgerow/js/ponds.js fun/hedgerow/js/levels/saint-clair.js fun/hedgerow/js/materials.js fun/hedgerow/js/groundmap.js fun/hedgerow/js/main.js fun/hedgerow/README.md && git commit -q -F - <<'EOF'\nHedgerow graphics: rainwater standing in the shell craters\n\nThe craters in the fields south of the village and in the forest were dry\nbowls of mud in the rain. Now the ones that hold water carry a pond\n(ponds.js, new; 31 of the level's 58): a disc at two fifths of the bowl's\ndepth, a little wider than the water so the bowl's own sides and rim cut\nits edge, all in one mesh drawn with the river's water material held\nstill (createWaterMaterial takes a `flow`; zero here): murky, mirroring\nthe sky and the fires, rain rings on it, browner in the shallows and a\nbroken line of scum where it laps the mud, both from its depth in the\nground map. The ground map keeps the grass, the stones and the twigs out\nof the ponds (createGroundMap takes them).\n\nThe level exports its craters (saint-clair.js `craters`: the same list\nthe terrain's bumps are made from, drawn in the same order, so the\nground is unchanged).\n\nThe water's direct specular is capped: the night's fill light is a\ndirectional light, and on still water it made a white-hot moon-like glint\nwherever the view faced it; the lamps and fires are mirrored by the\nscreen-space reflections anyway.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nEOF\ngit log --oneline -1 && (git merge-tree --write-tree --name-only hedgerow-poc hedgerow-grass >/dev/null 2>&1 && echo \"merges cleanly into hedgerow-poc\" || echo \"merge conflicts\")","description":"Commit the crater ponds"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"d310e29b-534b-4a51-ad9f-3614dbc29ed2","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgFiA4dT6vQrwbBGhkngf","requestRef":"712b2c86-63c5-4c5a-bfdf-33f5bcbe549b","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"840f4bf1-f603-46fc-8def-c15b5e02f61b","timestamp":"2026-10-21T16:38:02.100Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"max","perTurnEffort":"max","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/vojta/Dev/protocodus.github.io/.claude/worktrees/hedgerow-grass/fun/hedgerow","sessionId":"c33bf617-35bd-4ff6-a907-5e7d748d7fbc","version":"2.1.304","gitBranch":"hedgerow-poc","slug":"shimmying-swimming-falcon"}
