{"parentUuid":"6abd5001-4c8e-4e19-be15-7b5b9fa835b7","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgFiEGecoZznVVvPsymzW","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I made four more graphics commits on `hedgerow-grass`, each a separate improvement. Each was checked in a headless browser on the real GPU, the node checks pass, and each merges cleanly into `hedgerow-poc`. Nothing is pushed.\n\n- **4cd44831, flare glare fixed:** right under a flare the light could reach about 20 times its normal level and turn everything white. The flare's light on the ground is now soft-capped at about 3, which leaves a typical flare almost unchanged. Wet grass is also less glossy now, so the meadow no longer turns white; roads and puddles still mirror the flare.\n- **44873e66, muzzle flashes:** every rifle shot used to fill the whole view with orange haze for a frame. Flash lights now scatter only a quarter of their light into the air, so you see a flash at the muzzle with the rifle, hands and nearby street lit. I made this change in `lights.js`, so `player.js` is untouched.\n- **43fb454b, wheel ruts** (new `ruts.js`): the opening lane and the forest track now have two wheel ruts with a grassy strip between them and water standing in them in stretches. They have real depth up close. The cost is too small to measure.\n- **f4eb89a1, rainwater in shell craters** (new `ponds.js`): 31 of the 58 craters now hold still, murky water with rain rings, brown shallows and a scum line at the edge. Grass and stones are kept out of the water. I also capped the brightest highlights on all water, because the constant night fill light was making a white \"moon\" glint on still water.\n  - This commit edits the level file: `saint-clair.js` now exports its craters. The crater list comes out in the same order as before, so the terrain is unchanged and the world and route checks pass. If the original session also edits that file, this is the one commit that could conflict.\n\n**Things to know:**\n- I couldn't fully confirm the water highlight cap leaves the river looking the same, because a flare was burning in the \"after\" shots. The cap only trims the very brightest highlights, though.\n- The rule from before still applies: the anti-aliasing commit 2c09b946 must be merged together with its fix a0b204b2.\n\nThe shared notes list every commit. The test server, the headless browser and my `launch.json` entry are all removed."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":323,"cache_read_input_tokens":722340,"output_tokens":754,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":323,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":754,"cache_read_input_tokens":722340,"cache_creation_input_tokens":323,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":323},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"7a6c8f7e-0d74-4f51-88c3-55793eec0f3e","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgFiEFsjztoLAWinYc4Vi","requestRef":"7e807896-21fa-49b0-bb56-d92eb8013d24","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","attributionMcpServer":"ccd_turn","attributionMcpTool":"wrap_up","type":"assistant","uuid":"f93ebdf6-8bd6-4830-9ce6-8683e057abb7","timestamp":"2026-10-21T16:38:59.420Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"max","perTurnEffort":"max","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/vojta/Dev/protocodus.github.io/.claude/worktrees/hedgerow-grass","sessionId":"c33bf617-35bd-4ff6-a907-5e7d748d7fbc","version":"2.1.304","gitBranch":"hedgerow-poc","slug":"shimmying-swimming-falcon"}
