{"parentUuid":"139a4399-ed69-4227-b3d2-f7c06fe1f18f","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgFmZeZP3WsbktP9hjj98","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I made two more graphics commits on `hedgerow-grass`. Both were checked in a headless browser on the real GPU, the node checks pass, and both merge cleanly into `hedgerow-poc`. Nothing is pushed.\n\n- **bb3758d7, mud thrown over the view by a close blast:** a grenade within about 9 m now throws mud across the screen. You get big dark splats in the lower corners (kept clear of the rifle), smaller spiky ones and flecks round the edges, a wet glint on top, and some trickles running down. The closer the blast, the more mud, and it's gone after four seconds. Blasts in water don't do it.\n  - I confirmed it with a real grenade thrown 4 m from the player.\n  - This adds one line to `combat.js` (it calls `G.spatter`), plus the hook in `main.js` and the effect itself in `post.js`.\n- **1b150cc0, crowns of droplets where the rain lands:** within 7 m of the player, about 3,500 drops a second now each throw up a short-lived crown of droplets. They're dim grey, glint in lamplight and under flares, and are drawn after the anti-aliasing pass so they don't get smeared away. The wet cobbles now look like rain is hammering them. The cost is within measurement noise.\n\nThe shared notes list every commit. The test server, the headless browser and my `launch.json` entry are all removed."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":236,"cache_read_input_tokens":714795,"output_tokens":460,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":236,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":460,