{"parentUuid":"0313efb8-f5b8-4db3-a75a-2f8cc83613ed","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgFnZHt2iXYGsXGesGygW","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This round produced one commit on `hedgerow-grass`, and I tried and reverted a second idea. The commit was checked in a headless browser on the real GPU, the node checks pass, and it merges cleanly into `hedgerow-poc`. Nothing is pushed.\n\n**Committed: e22787ce, rain that comes in gusts.** The rain used to fall at one steady rate everywhere. Now bands of heavier rain about 30 m across blow downwind between lighter stretches, with the average rate unchanged.\n- In a gust the near streaks lean harder and all of them show. In a lull a light rain remains.\n- The far rain sheets follow the same pattern, so you see a gust coming down the street before it reaches you. The splashes and droplet crowns around the player thicken under it.\n- I confirmed it by working out a lull moment and a gust moment, then capturing both from the same spot: sparse thin rain in one, a slanted downpour in the other.\n- The cost is about 0.04 ms.\n\n**Tried and reverted: window glass reflecting the street.** I marked window panes as mirrors for the existing screen-space reflections, but the overlay showed rain streaks and grass edges getting mistakenly flagged as glass, and the panes themselves only showed a faint glint. Doing this properly needs a separate per-pixel mask, which is a bigger change, so I reverted it. The shared notes record the reason.\n\nThe test server, the headless browser and my `launch.json` entry are all removed."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":232,"cache_read_input_tokens":660067,"output_tokens":486,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation