{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"c33bf617-35bd-4ff6-a907-5e7d748d7fbc","hash":"d56bce73b59b87971de81795b68e15d8ffb5c70c5bbd798ca9541cc0414c3e53","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""},{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The crate obscures most of the curb, and where visible the stream looks nearly identical to the cobbles under this lighting, so it's not worth the extra code. I'll revert the change and note the reasoning.\n\n","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01NMP9cMd4GrmgnNkcWMncHL","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/vojta/Dev/protocodus.github.io/.claude/worktrees/hedgerow-grass && git checkout fun/hedgerow/js/ruts.js fun/hedgerow/js/terrain.js fun/hedgerow/js/main.js && git status --short && echo clean","description":"Revert the gutter experiment"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_016ER8FTZrAJp1p1p1emqQFb","name":"Edit","input":{"file_path":"/Users/vojta/Library/Application REDACTED.md","old_string":"so wet ground got flagged as glass in streaks; the window panes themselves gave only a faint\nglint at grazing angles. Would need a separate G-buffer bit, not the alpha.\n","new_string":"so wet ground got flagged as glass in streaks; the window panes themselves gave only a faint\nglint at grazing angles. Would need a separate G-buffer bit, not the alpha.\nTried and dropped: water running in the street's gutters (STREET in the ruts texture, a flat\nmirror strip along each cobble edge with downstream wavelets). Placed right, but under this\nlighting a flat dark stream reflecting dark house fronts is indistinguishable from the wet\ncobbles beside it in A/B captures; not worth the shader cost and complexity.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}]}}
