{"parentUuid":"4614917e-bea1-4a1c-873e-c11ce76cd078","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgFpW2Ywy2aCgUVN1npwB","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This round added two more commits on `hedgerow-grass`, and I tried and reverted one idea. Both commits were checked in a headless browser on the real GPU, the node checks pass, and both merge cleanly into `hedgerow-poc`. Nothing is pushed.\n\n- **ac6d826e, lit windows glowing in the rain:** light from the lit windows already fell on the street; now the rainy air in front of each window catches it too. A shop window or the café front stands in a warm haze, brightest when you look back into the window.\n  - The first version cost about 1 ms. I cut it to about 0.3–0.5 ms: fewer samples, the glow only out to 3.8 m, no glow from windows beyond 22 m, and skipping pixels too faint to see. That last cut mattered most, because the camera is often inside several window beams at once.\n- **ea7e6904, rain splashes seen by the light they catch:** the droplet crowns from the earlier round showed as bright white flecks even in the dark, which looked artificial in still frames. They're now faint where unlit and glint near lamps, fires and flares.\n- **Tried and reverted, water running in the street's gutters:** a flowing strip of water along each cobble edge. It sat in the right place, but in side-by-side captures it looked the same as the wet cobbles next to it, so it wasn't worth the extra shader code.\n\nThe branch is now 31 commits ahead of `hedgerow-poc`, and the shared notes list them all, including the failed experiments. The test server, the headless browser and my `launch.json` entry are all removed."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":252,"cache_read_input_tokens":787437,"output_tokens":515,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":252,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":515,"cache_read_input_tokens":787437,"cache_creation_input_tokens":252,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":252},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"33ec0739-79c8-45b5-956e-10f0c843c540","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgFpW1t1ETXvpjsikG94F","requestRef":"dc7fc7cf-a12e-4d6e-a4e8-e9ab2facd3a1","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","attributionMcpServer":"ccd_turn","attributionMcpTool":"wrap_up","type":"assistant","uuid":"e1c58088-a749-46db-8913-825f9b8fe455","timestamp":"2026-10-21T18:01:11.654Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"max","perTurnEffort":"max","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/vojta/Dev/protocodus.github.io/.claude/worktrees/hedgerow-grass","sessionId":"c33bf617-35bd-4ff6-a907-5e7d748d7fbc","version":"2.1.304","gitBranch":"hedgerow-poc","slug":"shimmying-swimming-falcon"}
