{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"c33bf617-35bd-4ff6-a907-5e7d748d7fbc","hash":"9569bec9c7a7ecb75e9b00ec90bcd4802655b6ba4829d2fec027f442f0ec3856","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""},{"type":"text","text":"Continuing with two more. First, grass that glows when backlit: the leaf transmission I added to tree foliage hasn't reached the meadow grass, which has its own material. Second, specular anti-aliasing on the terrain: the wet cobbles' relief makes distant highlights sparkle and crawl, and roughening the shading where the normal varies within a pixel is the standard fix. Starting with the grass."},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01HkgoFyNoTb8dgF9yccfPtH","name":"mcp__ccd_turn__update_plan","input":{"items":[{"content":"Grass glowing when backlit (leaf transmission)","status":"in_progress"},{"content":"Specular anti-aliasing on the wet ground","status":"pending"},{"content":"Verify headless; commit each","status":"pending"},{"content":"Clean up browsers and server","status":"pending"}],"scope":"continuation"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Wu4jdehah9DYva1j4W1Usu","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/vojta/Dev/protocodus.github.io/.claude/worktrees/hedgerow-grass/fun/hedgerow && grep -n \"RE_Direct_Leaf\\|leafThin\\|uLeafTrans\" -n js/materials.js | head; sed -n 150,175p js/grass.js","description":"Read the leaf transmission and the grass fragment hooks"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}]}}
